// How many tests each assembly may skip on a desk with the SSH fixture up (QS136).
//
// A skip past these numbers fails run-tests.cmd, so a new one is a decision written here with its
// reason rather than weather nobody reads. The fixture's own skips are not counted against them
// only where a run declares it has none (QUICKSHELL_NO_FIXTURE, which the guest runner sets); a
// desk that forgot to start it is over budget. A test only the guest can run, whose skip names a
// tools/provision-guest-*.ps1 script, is waived off the guest and counted in it (QS291), so these
// numbers do not carry the guest's provisioning.
{
  // The PuTTY sessions and the MobaXterm.ini a real machine may hold: nothing to read on a clean desk.
  // Three since QS297 put a second test on the real MobaXterm.ini (QS355): one for PuTTY, two for it.
  "Quickshell.App.Tests": 3,

  // run-fuzz.cmd's findings, which a desk that never fuzzed does not have.
  "Quickshell.Terminal.Tests": 1,

  // The Windows ssh-agent service, off unless somebody started it; and QS139's reproduction, kept
  // skipped until SSH.NET bounds a channel's window.
  "Quickshell.Transport.Tests": 2
}
